      "text": "Requirements:\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Requirements:\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "iH0FezjOlZIJ5NWuM-VtZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 635.6806850320261,
      "y": 540.0539430750607,
      "width": 746.779541015625,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 64708259,
      "version": 467,
      "versionNonce": 563965219,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "6-Eb_vz32w9k1V0DLUmQi",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785229491436,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Extensible\n\n1. What log levels are supported?\n    - INFO, WARN, ERROR and We should be able to add new log levels later.\n\n2. What should be the output destination of the message?\n    - Console, File but It should be extensible\n\n3. In what format should we log the message?\n    - Plain Text and JSON Again, it should be extensible",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Extensible\n\n1. What log levels are supported?\n    - INFO, WARN, ERROR and We should be able to add new log levels later.\n\n2. What should be the output destination of the message?\n    - Console, File but It should be extensible\n\n3. In what format should we log the message?\n    - Plain Text and JSON Again, it should be extensible",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XYjGe8zuSgGVh1yvFoKbk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 626.8401546505087,
      "y": 825.2031912008918,
      "width": 802.799560546875,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 638364515,
      "version": 72,
      "versionNonce": 1561681677,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785228660019,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High Traffic\n\n1. Should the logger work correctly when multiple threads log at the same time?\n - Yes\n    Example: If Thread 1 wants to log \"World\" and Thread 2 wants to log \"Shubh\",\n                The output should not become: Sworldhubh",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High Traffic\n\n1. Should the logger work correctly when multiple threads log at the same time?\n - Yes\n    Example: If Thread 1 wants to log \"World\" and Thread 2 wants to log \"Shubh\",\n                The output should not become: Sworldhubh",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
